  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: a4f57265f2d95884493f924517248368, type: 3}
  m_Name: OldMan 3
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::DialougeText
  paragraphs:
  - Huh? Oh right, right. So yeah this temple. Big lookin' thing, all fancy, lotta
    people.
  - 'Anyway at the end of every August before the spring they''d choose one student
    to sip from the "Drink of Life" as they called it. '
  - Some black liquid from a paper cup. Nasty lookin' stuff. Said to give the drinker
    amazing powers.
  - Or kill them, can't remember. Fifty fifty I guess.
  - Anyway them traditionalists would always make a big show out of it, celebrations
    and music and what have you.
  - 'Me and my friends would sneak into the scrub land off the asphalt drive they''d
    be celebrating. '
  - One year though, they had some scrawny lookin' fella up there on that podium.
    And they revealed the liquid with the reverence for him to drink.
  - Its said to watch was a sin or somethin' so everyone had this purple cloth over
    there heads as they sat and prayed and the drums banged on.
  - In that moment, I had a wicked thought. Curiosity will kill ya'know and it should
    have killed me.
  - 'I leaped from the bushes and in that moment of pause while nobody was looking
    I swiped the drink out from the kids claws and tossed it back right there on
    stage. '
  - It tasted like tar and grease and what have you, very unpleasent.
  - And the kid was swearing and screaming, tossing a fit.
  - So I ducked out of the scene and they chased me up and down the streets. I ended
    up skipping town and they never really followed me.
  - I guess they were stuck in there little building i guess.
